   "text": "I read this as a cyclic lipopeptide: a 3-hydroxyhexadecanoyl chain on a Glu\u2013Orn tail, attached to a macrocycle closed by an ester to a Tyr phenol oxygen. I assigned each stereocentre from the wedges and hashes in the drawing. The 3-hydroxy carbon of the fatty chain has plain bonds, so it carries no stereo label.\n\n**Lipid tail.** I counted the chain from the amide carbonyl: C1 is the C=O, C2 is CH2, C3 is CH(OH), and C4\u2013C16 run up to the terminal CH3. That makes a 3-hydroxyhexadecanoyl group.\n\n**Side chain.** The lipid is acylated onto a Glu (free \u03b3-COOH), which is linked to an Orn (free \u03b4-NH2). The Orn carbonyl then forms the amide to the Tyr that closes the ring.\n\n**Macrocycle.** Going around the ring from that Tyr:\n- Tyr: its benzylic CH2 is drawn as \"C\", and the para oxygen forms the ester ring closure.\n- Thr: alpha carbon plus a CH(CH3)OH side chain.\n- Glu: free \u03b3-COOH.\n- Ala.\n- Pro.\n- Gln: side-chain primary amide.\n- Tyr: free para-OH.\n- Ile: its carbonyl is esterified by the first Tyr's phenol oxygen.\n\nSMILES: CCCCCCCCCCCCCC(O)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@H](CCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H]1Cc2ccc(cc2)OC(=O)[C@H]([C@H](C)CC)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2ccc(O)cc2)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@@H]2CCCN2C(=O)[C@@H](C)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(=O)O)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@H](C)O)NC1=O"
